      "problem": "The volume of a cube is $64\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
      "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{64\\,000}=40\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $40\\,\\text{cm}.$",
